\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Six real Snowy Scenes val-split frames run through the trained checkpoint: three \texttt  {accumulated} (nominal) and three \texttt  {falling} (degraded), each showing the camera image, LiDAR BEV occupancy channel, and the CCP disagreement map $1-S$. Mean disagreement is consistently \emph  {higher} for the visually milder \texttt  {accumulated} frames (category mean $0.590$) than the visually more severe \texttt  {falling} frames (category mean $0.565$) --- the wrong-direction pattern this section diagnoses, visible here across six independent real frames rather than only in aggregate.}}{21}{figure.25}\protected@file@percent }
